---
description: Godot 4 GDScript style and API rules
globs: "**/*.gd"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Godot 4 syntax only: `@export`, `@onready`, `await`, `signal.emit()`, `signal.connect(callable)`, `CharacterBody2D`/`3D`.
- Type every variable, parameter and return value. `-> void` on functions that return nothing.
- `CharacterBody2D`: set `velocity`, then call `move_and_slide()` with no arguments.
- Use `Input.get_vector("move_left", "move_right", "move_up", "move_down")` for movement; action names come from the Input Map.
- Expose tuning values with `@export` (and `@export_range` where sensible) instead of magic numbers.
- Prefer signals and groups to absolute node paths. Avoid `get_parent().get_parent()`.
- Free nodes with `queue_free()`, never `free()`, during gameplay.
- Keep scripts under ~200 lines; split behaviour into child nodes/components when they grow.
